{#-
Advance Scene: rewrites a scene value for the current point of the story
(talemate.agents.creator.advance_scene).

Variables:
  - info_type: scene_description, story_intention, phase_intention,
    description_override, intention_override (what each one is, and how it is
    written, is in advance-scene/<info-type>.jinja2)
  - info_label: what is rewritten, as the prompt calls it
  - info_title: what is rewritten, as the world editor calls it
  - target_name: whose override it is (a character, a group, or several
    characters sharing it), none for the scene's own values
  - characters: [{name, sheet, description}], as the prompt may see them
  - locations: where people are
  - states: the state reinforcements, as context lines
  - context_values: [{title, value}], the values rewritten before this one
  - scene_type: {name, description} of the current scene, if there is one
  - old_value: the value to rewrite
  - paragraphs, words: how long the answer may be

Extractors:
  - response: AnchorExtractor("<ANSWER>", "</ANSWER>", fallback_to_full=True)
-#}
{% set subject = info_label ~ (" for " ~ target_name if target_name else "") -%}
{# RENDERED CONTEXT #}
{% set rendered_context -%}
<|SECTION:QUICK SUMMARY OF TASK TO COMPLETE|>
Update the old {{ subject }} so that it matches the current point in time of the story, rather than the start of the story.

More instructions are given below in the task section.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
<|SECTION:CHARACTERS|>
{% for character in characters %}
### {{ character.name }}
{{ character.sheet }}

{{ character.description }}
{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% for item in context_values %}
<|SECTION:{{ item.title|upper }}|>
{{ item.value }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endfor %}
{% if locations or states %}
<|SECTION:ADDITIONAL INFORMATION|>
{% if locations %}
{{ locations }}

{% endif %}
{% for state in states %}
{{ state }}

{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}
{% endset %}
{# END RENDERED CONTEXT #}

{# PREPARE SCENE HISTORY #}
{% set rendered_context_tokens = count_tokens(rendered_context) + count_tokens(old_value) %}
{% set history_budget = max(max_tokens - 600 - rendered_context_tokens - words * 2, 256) %}
{% set scene_history = scene.context_history(budget=history_budget, keep_context_investigation=False) -%}
{% set final_line_number = len(scene_history) %}
{# END PREPARE SCENE HISTORY #}

{{ rendered_context }}
<|SECTION:SCENE|>
Events and dialogue in chronological order, from the top (oldest) to the bottom (newest).

{% for scene_context in scene_history -%}
{{ loop.index }}. {{ scene_context }}
{% endfor -%}
{% if not scene_history -%}
No dialogue so far
{% endif -%}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>

{% include "writing-style-instructions.jinja2" %}

<|SECTION:TASK|>
Rewrite and update the following value, the {{ subject }}, so that it matches the current state of the story so far. The old {{ info_label }} dealt with the beginning of the story, but now it is out of date and not completely related to what is happening at the present time in the story.

{% include "advance-scene/" ~ (info_type|replace("_", "-")) ~ ".jinja2" %}

Consider the entire context and honor the sequentiality of the dialogue. Answer based on the final state of the dialogue.

Progression of the dialogue is important. The last line is the most important, the first line is the least important.
{% if final_line_number %}

Respect the scene progression and answer in the context of line {{ final_line_number }}.
{% endif %}

Use your imagination to fill in gaps in order to generate the {{ info_label }} in a confident and decisive manner. Avoid uncertainty and vagueness.
{% if target_name -%}
Write it only from what is known to {{ target_name }}: leave out anything not witnessed by or told to {{ target_name }}.
{%- else -%}
You are omniscient and can describe the scene in detail.
{%- endif %}


Provide your answer wrapped in <ANSWER> tags like this: <ANSWER>your answer here</ANSWER>

Previous {{ info_label }} value to rewrite (the full value, wrapped in a code block):

```
{{ old_value }}
```

Again, as a reminder, your answer must be wrapped in <ANSWER> tags like this: <ANSWER>your answer here</ANSWER>

{# its own length instruction: the client doesn't add its generic one #}
{{- set_response_length_instructions() -}}
The length of your response must fit within {{ paragraphs }} paragraph{% if paragraphs != 1 %}s{% endif %} (about {{ words }} words).
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{{ set_prepared_response("<ANSWER>") }}
